    },
    "shadow-tint-4": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": "color-mix(in oklab, var(--ink) 14%, transparent)"
    },
    "elevation-card": {
      "$type": "dimension",
      "$value": "0 1px 2px var(--shadow-tint-1), 0 4px 12px var(--shadow-tint-1)",
      "$extensions": {
        "silvicom.section": [
          "D-DR2: a card's edge is its SHADOW, not a drawn line. `0 1px 2px` at 5% ink is invisible at arm's length, which left `ring-edge-subtle` doing all the work and made every card read as outlined rather than lifted. The second, wider layer is what the comps use to separate a white card from a near-white canvas without a line. The ring stays — it is the fallback under `prefers-contrast: more`, where shadows carry nothing.",
          "elevation — shadows carry depth so cards and overlays do not need dark perimeters"
        ],
        "silvicom.expose": "shadow"
      }
    },
    "elevation-card-raised": {
      "$type": "dimension",
